# An SSH server, for looking at this machine from another one.
#
# Not in the base image on purpose: a desktop does not need to be reachable, and
# ADR-0012 keeps the base a desktop rather than a workstation.
#
# The live session is the awkward case. live-config creates the account and
# Strata logs straight into it, so nothing ever asks for a password and nobody
# is told what it is. Starting sshd there would expose an account whose
# credentials the owner does not know — so the component sets neither a password
# nor a key, and says what to do instead.
SUMMARY="OpenSSH server, so another machine can reach this one"
CATEGORY="diagnostics"
ORIGIN="debian"
PACKAGES="openssh-server"
POST_INSTALL="systemctl disable --now ssh"
NOTE="Not started. On a live session the account has a password nobody was told, so start it only after setting one: 'sudo passwd user', then 'sudo systemctl start ssh'. Better, copy a key over first and set PasswordAuthentication no."
